    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Magician</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Magician is a combination of introversion, egocentrism, rationality, and calmness. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to the sciences, journalism, literature, and philosophy. With their innovative nature, Magicians are easily the paragons in the field. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them. </p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/engineer.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Engineer/Scientist</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Magicians are best suited as pioneers. Because they have the natural knack to shape reality as they see fit, they’ll find it natural to create new innovations and participate in humanity’s progress. </p>
              <p>With your trait being the Magician, you are best suited to being at the frontier of human wisdom. Your bold outlook and your enterprising mind will prove crucial in engineering and sciences.</p>
              <p>A necessary trait for the pursuit of science is curiosity, and the Magician-- being a person whose very existence desires to challenge reality itself, is understandably an easy fit. Since you naturally want truth and desire nothing more than to use it to your advantage, your studies and research will certainly help advance any modern theories on biology or physics.</p>
              <p>In fact, you can even go beyond just being a researcher and actually focus your mind on science’s more social applications. This means you can pursue economics, for example, and craft theories and ways to change your country’s way of advancing its economy. With your naturally crafty attitude, you won’t just be satisfying your inner thirst for knowledge, your community will also love you!</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>In addition to this, you also have a calm side to you. This will be very useful when confronted with difficult deadlines, such as those that engineers might face in the process of making new structures. Since you have a tranquil attitude, your presence will do more than just reassure others; you will also be able to offer real solutions or alternatives that will actively ease the stress your teammates might go through.</p>
          <p>Lastly, both jobs fit naturally into your introverted nature. Since you are the sort of person who will work alone when given a chance, you will naturally thrive at these particular jobs, often asking you to work without any supervision or guidance. Combined with your analytical mind and a heart for truth and creativity, there is no limit to what you can accomplish in these fields. However demanding, you will always find a reason to go beyond what’s expected of you.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/journalist.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Journalist/Reporter</h5>
              <p>If there is one thing that a Magician treasures most, it’s information. After all, information gives way to knowledge and perspective. The more knowledgeable one becomes of their surroundings, the deeper their understanding will be of reality. This then allows people to have opinions about their current reality or even change it.</p>
              <p>As such, it’s easy to figure out why journalism would be a Magician’s cup of tea. The job itself offers you a lot of opportunities to learn how society works across all levels. It will expose you to all kinds of knowledge as well, and you are tasked with making sure that the knowledge you gain is digestible enough for a democratic public to read. The higher you rise through the ranks, the tougher the work. But you are well-equipped to face such challenges.</p>
              <p>Aside from knowledge, journalism will also improve your already strong command of the language. Since journalism aims to disseminate information in the process of speaking truth to power, you will be asked to write in unique ways to bring the story to the public. Your eloquence will play a huge role in making sure this happens.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>That besides, it’s also going to involve a lot of teamwork that will ultimately help mitigate your otherwise proud, individualistic nature. While working for the press, you will be meeting all kinds of characters who will test your patience and be the best in the field. To thrive, you will need to get rid of any preconceptions you have and work with them.</p>
          <p>However, the most important reason you can be a journalist is that you ultimately get to keep your principles as a Magician. You will be allowed to truly make opinions that are relevant to our time and have them known to the public through a democratic platform. Thus, you are in a position to actively influence how the times work.</p>
          <p>In a rather important age such as this, the call to journalism is a naturally strong one. As a Magician, you are uniquely suited for this role because you have both the curiosity and drive to truly make the world a more positive place. By informing the public and enlightening them, you will be doing everyone you know a service.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/writer.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Writer</h5>
              <p>In terms of creativity, the Magician’s potential is without bounds. Their minds are very childlike and will often wander around in search of something that would stimulate their creative faculties. One can see from this yet another career path a Magician can take: writer.</p>
              <p>Throughout human history, one thing has always persisted: the written word. Its very capacity to preserve itself-- and be preserved by those who wish to maintain traditions or a national sense of identity-- makes it a truly formidable tool that one can use to leave a mark on the world. In a way, writing is all about leaving a legacy, and in the right hands, a pen can change the world.</p>
              <p>For many writers, there are several ways to create a legacy. They can either articulate their thoughts to accurately portray the human condition as is the case with many literary works, or they can write their thoughts on the important issues of the day and hope that their thoughts can be used to change the world one way or another.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>But while the path is indeed open, many writers often struggle to find their inner voice. This is where the Magician truly holds an edge. By nature, Magicians are filled to the brim with ideas-- and whatever empty sheets of paper there might be, they are more than capable of ensuring that it won’t stay that way for long. If anything, you might be the kind of person who asks for more paper to write stuff!</p>
          <p>In a way, then, it could be said that you were necessarily born for this kind of task. You may still struggle with words right now, but your natural eloquence will carry you through any hardship if you do pursue this path.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
